<p>Tryouts were held each spring at the {% place "mandan-memorial-building" %}World War Memorial Building{% endplace %}, now Mandan City Hall, to fill 80 cast roles. The 2,000-seat amphitheater, equipped with a 110-foot stage, hosted the production from July 1 through Labor Day, with performances Wednesday through Sunday. Professional actors from cities such as Duluth and Chicago were recruited for approximately six leading roles. The 1959 production budget was {% inflation 75000, 1959 %}, raised by local merchants, citizens, and fraternal and civic organizations.</p>

