<h3>Mandan Historical Development Association</h3>

<p>The Mandan Historical Development Association was organized on September 23, 1958, to promote and develop the historical advantages of Mandan and the surrounding area. Its primary task was producing the outdoor drama. The Chamber of Commerce selected the first board of directors, and members elected later directors at annual meetings. In 1962, responsibility for operating the drama passed to the Mandan Development Corporation (MDC). The corporation worked to promote Mandan's economic development and assist businesses financially. Continuing the play was an effort to strengthen area tourism. The MDC and Chamber discontinued the production after the 1968 season when attendance declined and there was insufficient public support for a major renovation of the fort's amphitheater.</p>

